{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Morning, Mr Pillay. Come through, the doctor's just finishing. I'll do your blood pressure while we wait.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Howzit. Ag, I'm fine. My wife panics over a lump in the groin, it comes up when I lift at work and then it's gone.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): Sleeve up for me, please.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Those robots by the parking were hectic, hey. Bakkie's half in the road.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (NURSE): Ja, chaos out there. Blood pressure is one forty eight over ninety two. Pulse is seventy eight. Oxygen is ninety eight percent.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Not bad, hey. I've worked through worse.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (NURSE): It's still a bit up. My sister's pressure was a proper mess last year, three tablets, and she gave up salt completely. The doctor can talk about yours.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Eish, not me. One tablet and I'm lekker.",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (DOCTOR): Mr Pillay, sorry to keep you waiting. Doctor Mokoena. I had a look at the numbers the sister took. What's brought you in?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): The lump. Right in the groin. She booked me, I wouldn't have come.",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (DOCTOR): Which side did you say?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Right. Left side is fine, nothing there.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (DOCTOR): When did this start? Any date you remember?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm, err, no. I can't put a date on it. A few months, maybe before the December shutdown, maybe after. I never wrote it down.",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (DOCTOR): Right, so the start date is uncertain. A few months is as close as we'll get. What do you do for work?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): Construction. Bricklaying, bags of cement, crates of tiles. Been at it since I left school.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (DOCTOR): And the lump, it comes out with that lifting?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja. When I lift it pops right out, about a golf ball, maybe smaller. Same one for these few months.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (DOCTOR): What about when you lie down?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): When I lie down it goes away. Slides back in. I lie in the bakkie at lunch and it's gone.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (DOCTOR): Is it painful?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Not really. Not sore, I don't have pain.",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any vomiting? Or nausea?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): No vomiting. Never. And I'm not nauseous either.",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any fever? Change in the bowels, constipation or diarrhoea?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): No fever. Bowels are the same as always. Not that either.",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (DOCTOR): Burning when you pass water, or trouble getting it going?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Not really. It's normal.",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any long-standing conditions? Diabetes, asthma, high blood pressure?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): High blood pressure for about twelve years. No diabetes. Not asthma either. I mostly ignore the pressure.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (DOCTOR): Known hypertension, ongoing. Not diabetes. What is the tablet called, and the dose?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): Amlodopine. I nearly said ten, uh no, five milligrams. Once in the morning, by mouth, for the pressure.",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (DOCTOR): Do you take it every day as prescribed, or do you miss some?",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Mm, I suppose.",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (DOCTOR): That's not a clear yes. I'm not sure you take it the way it was prescribed. Any headaches with the blood pressure, or dizziness?",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): No... well, sometimes. A mild headache in the late afternoon. Not dizzy, not that.",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (DOCTOR): Chest pain? Short of breath when you lift or climb stairs?",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): No chest pain. Breathing is fine, not that either.",
  "[SEG0039] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any allergies to medicines? Rash, swelling?",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Never. Nothing like that.",
  "[SEG0041] person_3 (DOCTOR): Have you had operations before?",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Never been cut.",
  "[SEG0043] person_3 (DOCTOR): You said there was no pain. By the evening, after a shift, what happens?",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (PATIENT): Ag, well. By evening there's a mild ache in the groin. I sit down and it settles. It's nothing, really.",
  "[SEG0045] person_3 (DOCTOR): Has the lump been getting bigger?",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (PATIENT): Sometimes, not really. I couldn't say. I don't look at it that hard.",
  "[SEG0047] person_3 (DOCTOR): Not a clear answer, so I won't call it enlarging. Lie back and cough for me. Soft lump in the right groin, it reduces when you lie flat, and the cough impulse is there. No redness, skin looks normal, abdomen soft and not tender.",
  "[SEG0048] person_2 (PATIENT): See? Nothing to stress about.",
  "[SEG0049] person_3 (DOCTOR): Let me think out loud. It comes out when you strain, goes back when you lie down, there's a mild ache by evening, and you're not vomiting. A bit of fat, or sometimes bowel, pushes through a weak spot in the groin muscle, that's how a hernia works.",
  "[SEG0050] person_2 (PATIENT): Mm. Not cancer, though.",
  "[SEG0051] person_3 (DOCTOR): I don't think it's cancer. My working impression is a right inguinal hernia, provisional until the surgeons confirm it. I'm referring you to general surgery, and that will be booked.",
  "[SEG0052] person_2 (PATIENT): Can I still lift tomorrow?",
  "[SEG0053] person_3 (DOCTOR): No heavy lifting, and no cement bags, until they have seen you. If the lump will not go back in, or you start vomiting, go to casualty the same day. If you have not heard from the surgeons in a month, come back and see me."
 ],
